1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,700
Imagine waking up to a world without birds.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,100
No dawn chorus.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,500
No wings against the sky.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,300
The silence is only the beginning.

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,000
First, insects could surge.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Many birds eat vast numbers of insects,

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
helping keep populations in check.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,450
Without them, crops and forests would face greater pressure.

9
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,000
Then, plants would feel the loss.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,600
Some depend on birds to carry pollen or spread seeds.

11
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:30,650
Their forests could slowly change, and struggle to renew.

12
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,800
Scavenger birds clean up carcasses.

13
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,000
Without them, decay would linger longer,

14
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
and the risk of disease could rise in some places.

15
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,500
From oceans to cities, food webs would shift.

16
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,600
Predators would lose their prey,

17
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,100
and ecosystems would have to find a new balance.

18
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,800
A world without birds would be quieter, but also more fragile.

19
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,100
Protect their habitats today,

20
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,200
and keep the sky alive tomorrow.
